Description: Free, world-class voice-to-text for Ubuntu, macOS and Windows
 Voice to Text is a push-to-talk offline voice transcription app that runs the
 Whisper model in-process for sub-second latency. The model loads once at
 startup and remains resident, eliminating the subprocess spawn tax that
 previous releases paid on every key press.
 .
 Features:
  - Push-to-talk recording (Scroll Lock by default, configurable)
  - In-process Whisper via whisper-rs — no Python runtime, no pip install
  - GPU acceleration via Vulkan (NVIDIA, AMD, and Intel GPUs)
  - GGML models downloaded on demand from the whisper.cpp upstream
  - Default small.en model pre-downloaded by postinst (~488 MB)
  - System tray with GTK3 and libappindicator
  - 100% offline operation after the model is cached
 .
 2.0.x ships a pre-built binary for amd64, because Ubuntu LTS cargo
 1.75 cannot parse the edition-2024 Cargo.toml manifests that modern
 Rust dependencies use. The binary is compiled on Emmanuel's machine
 with Rust 1.91 and committed to the source tree. See debian/rules
 for rationale.
 .
 2.0.0 breaking changes from the 1.0.x C binary:
  - Replaces CTranslate2 / faster-whisper Python backend with whisper-rs
  - Replaces the legacy C binary with the Rust rewrite
  - Python 3 is no longer required
  - Existing CT2 model caches are not reused; GGML models download on first use
